# Both hold an API key that can write attendance for the whole group. The
# runner carries it as an environment variable so the config stays readable by
# whoever maintains the box; see bridge/run-bridge.example.bat.
bridge/config.toml
bridge/run-bridge.bat
bridge/*.sqlite3
bridge/*.log

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Factor HR exports — salary, PAN, Aadhaar, bank details for the whole group.
# Never commit these. The directory is tracked; its contents are not.
# Git will not descend into an excluded directory, so directories have to be
# re-included before a file inside one can be.
data/**
!data/**/
!data/**/README.md

# The dashboard. `.env` names the site and the desk; node_modules and dist are
# both rebuilt by `npm install` and `npm run build`.
node_modules/
client/.env
client/dist/
# `wrangler dev`'s local state — a simulated edge, not anything deployed.
client/.wrangler/

# **The built bundle is committed and the sourcemap is not.**
#
# `manna_hr/public/hr/` and `manna_hr/www/hr.html` are `npm run build`'s output,
# and they are in the repo on purpose: `bench get-app` has to be able to serve
# the dashboard on a site with no node on it. The sourcemap is the one piece
# that is not needed to serve it — three and a half megabytes, larger than the
# rest of the repo put together, and it publishes every source file and comment
# at a URL anybody can read.
manna_hr/public/**/*.map

# Bundles and scratch. `*.bundle` is how a batch of commits gets carried
# between machines when neither can reach the other's remote — a transport,
# not a source. `_claude/` and `Claude outputs/` are the staging area for the
# same journey: copies of files that land in the tree properly, and
# screenshots of them. Committing either duplicates the repo inside itself.
*.bundle
_claude/
Claude outputs/
